# The ONE line that the production box's /home/acb/.ssh/authorized_keys gets
# for the staging box (WS-38 §5.3 and T-9). Replace KEY with the public half of
# /home/acb/.ssh/staging_link on the staging box. The key can forward one port,
# the Console, and can read the staging export folder, and nothing else: no
# shell, no pty, no agent, no X11, no other port.
#
# ⚠️ `port-forwarding` turns on REMOTE forwarding (-R) too, and `permitopen`
# limits -L only. Without `permitlisten`, a holder of this key could bind a
# free loopback port on the production box, and hold 8080 or 8090 while that
# unit restarts. `permitlisten="127.0.0.1:1"` is the one port it may listen on,
# and acb cannot bind a port below 1024. So -R binds no TCP port.
#
# ⚠️ It does NOT stop a Unix-socket -R (streamlocal): OpenSSH has no per-key
# rule for that. The production sshd_config closes it for acb, and sshd -t
# checks the file before the reload:
#   Match User acb
#       AllowStreamLocalForwarding no
restrict,port-forwarding,permitopen="127.0.0.1:8090",permitlisten="127.0.0.1:1",command="/usr/bin/rrsync -ro /var/lib/acb-staging-export/current" KEY acb-staging-link
